                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "To explain why Democrats and Republicans have come to so deeply distrust one another, we must consider not only their continual disagreements on the issues of the day but also the divergent values and principles that motivate them, the distinct constituencies that support them, and the accelerating history of conflict between them.",
